WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.334
-Paula, we've been friends
for a long time,

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.667
and I always love
having you on the show.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.901
-I love it.
-You did one bit when we were on

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:08.667
the Zoom shows, and thank you
for being a guest,

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:11.267
where you fake froze
on the screen.

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:14.167
-Yep.
-And, honestly, I didn't see it

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.834
done before, and I take all
of your bits, and I do them.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.234
I try to give you credit
for all the time I take them.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:19.501
-And I'm sure you do them
better than me.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:21.567
-No, I do not.
But can you show everyone

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:22.901
what it's like to do a freeze.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.167
-Like, what camera
would be best?

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.300
-This one here, camera one.
-This -- one?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.567
Okay.
-Here we go.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.567
How was --
How was your spring?

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.234
Any summer --
-It was good, Jimmy.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:33.033
I mean, you know, we're
in quarantine and everything,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.868
but I've been
trying to learn guitar,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.434
and I've been trying to do
a little more singing.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:40.167
So, I --
Oh, I --

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:45.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.501 --> 00:01:00.901
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:03.767
That's exactly --
That's exactly right.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:06.400
That's how you do it.
That's exactly right.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is how you do it.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.267
That is a pro.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.701
Thank you for doing that.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.667
How many bits have we done
together through out the years?

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.834
-We have done so many bits.
And you know, we used to do bits

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:17.434
on "SNL" because we didn't know
what we were going to write.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:19.634
Or we were writing something
that was not going well.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.033
-Do you remember the one where
we used to do a bit

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:25.033
where we'd say something --
we'd get fake mad at each other,

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.634
and say the worst thing
you could ever say to someone,

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.968
and then we would leave
and slam the door.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.334
And then you have to sheepishly
come back in, and get your keys.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.567
-Yeah, I'm gonna show you
right now.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.801
You've all done it when you've
had a fight with your spouse

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.501
or a family member.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.367
You really have a good exit.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:43.400
You really, really
leave on a good note of, like,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.601
"You're dead to me,"

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.400
and then you have
to come back in for something.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.667
So, here it is.
-All right. So what are --

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.767
-You know what, Jimmy?

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:53.634
I'm really sick of your
pretty-boy, charm box

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.000
bull crap, okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.067
-Really?
-No, I'm sick of it.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:01.067
I have -- I've --
I've put on a fake smile

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:04.434
all these years with you,
and I am done!

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.667
I am done with you!

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.367
I'm -- I'm outta here!
I'm outta here!

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:10.367
-Okay.
-All right?

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.501
-Gosh.
-Is this the exit?

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:13.968
[ Laughter ]
I'm done!

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:18.100
I don't ever
want to see you again.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.701
-Okay.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.300
That was weird.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.701
-I forgot my phone.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.234
-Yeah, you forgot your phone.
Yeah.

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:33.801
-In this time that I was gone,
I thought about things.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:37.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.868
And I'm sorry.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:43.067
-Yeah, okay.
-I -- I'm --

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.701
I'm sorry.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.567
I've had three coffees.
I'm a little constipated.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.567
I am jacked up.
I'm sorry that I went there.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.534
Okay? I'm sorry.
I forgive you.

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:54.801
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.601
Forgive me?
-Yeah.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.000
-Forgive me?
I should forgive you!

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.167
-Forgive me?
-Yeah, oh, for -- yeah.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.400
Oh, yeah!
Forgive you for being

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.567
the biggest loser that's ever
been on my show, ever!

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.634
-That's spit!
-Yeah, it is spit!

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.200
I spit right there.
And guess what!

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.234
You're husband's
cheating on you, you idiot!

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.434
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:19.300
-Well, tell my
lesbian wife that!

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:26.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.300
-Hi.
-Hi.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.834
-I, uh...

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:43.300
I just forgot
I have to finish --

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.667
finish hosting the show.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:46.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:48.400
And I had some time
to think about what I said.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.167
That was silly of me,
and I was out of line.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.200
I don't know
what I even was saying.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.868
And, uh...

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.234
I forgive you.
-I forgive you.

00:03:57.234 --> 00:04:00.334
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.567
-And scene.

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.868
And that's a scene.
[ Laughing ]

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:06.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.901
"Tell my --
Tell my lesbian wife that."

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.667
-"Tell my lesbian wife that!"

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.567
[ Laughter ]
Sorry, Mom.

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:13.734
It's the first
she's heard of it.

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.734
-Oh, wow!

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:19.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.334
Paula, let's talk about --
-This is the good view for --

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.667
This is a good angle, right?
For talk shows?

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:24.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.367
-Let's talk about "Girls5eva."

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:27.767
-Okay, let's talk about
"Girls5eva."

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.701
-"Girls5eva" -- it's on Peacock.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.667
-Oh, it's such a fun show.
-It is a fun show.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:33.467
It's a musical show.

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:36.100
Basically, it's a girl group
from the '90s that reunite.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.734
-Yeah.
-And they are underdogs.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.634
-Yep, we were a one-hit wonder,

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:44.968
and then a rapper
sampled one of our songs.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.601
Probably the only hit
we ever had.

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:49.334
-Yeah.
-And so we're trying to --

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:50.734
You know,
we're really underdogs.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:53.701
We're trying to get it back,
and we storm the stage

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:56.634
at the end of last season
at Jingle Ball.

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:59.367
And so we ended up
with a record deal,

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:00.634
which is very exciting.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.667
So this season
is all about album mode.

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:06.067
We're making a record,
but it is with Property Records,

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.234
which is owned
by the Property Brothers.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:09.601
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:12.367
-So it's a little low-end.
-No, but everyone's --

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:13.767
People are doing a lot things
these days.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:15.033
-Yes.
-So the Property Brothers

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:17.234
have a record label.
-Yes, and it's not low-end

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.834
because of the Property Brothers
being low-end,

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:21.601
'cause they're fabulous, but --
I watch them all the time.

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:24.334
But they haven't
been in the music industry.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.834
Music space, as they call it.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:28.467
Is that what they call it,
The Roots? The space?

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:31.501
-Do they show up in the season?
Can we say?

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:33.434
-They show up some
in the season,

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:35.400
and we have
a lot of fun guest stars.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.968
And there's a lot of
funny songs this season.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:41.701
And there's also --

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:44.767
This summer before we shot,
I actually

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:47.901
had my knee replacement
that I got five years ago.

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:51.634
I got two knee replacements,
and one of them collapsed.

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:54.701
And so I had to get
another knee replacement.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:56.133
So they wrote that
into the show.

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.334
So there's a whole element
at the beginning of the season

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:03.067
where I hurt my knee in a very
comedy way that you will enjoy.

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:04.634
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:07.534
Here's Paula Pell in the new
season of "Girls5eva."

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:10.267
-And this is after I'm trying
